# L §5.14 The take is a fill over arcs (2.1-C7b-22): the demands at one point are "in the day's first batch, every
# outflow at x of its pads at the start, observations and plans ...; at a decision's point, that decision's outflows
# ...; at a reading's point after a decision, or at the close, that reading's pad".  konto holds Ania's 100.00 and
# Tomek's 50.00, its order Ania's first.  The decision out takes 30.00 on 2026-03-01 (from Ania's); the reading
# `after out` states 100.00, so its pad takes the gap of 20.00 at its own point, by the leaving rule, from Ania's:
# Ania 50.00, Tomek 50.00 (scratch/exp_r3.py).
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
kind persons: parties
kind savings: place PLN min 0
  owned by arrive
  step minor(PLN)
  takes k for w order (if k.owner == ania then 0 else 1)
kind tomeks: transfers
place konto: savings lives 2026-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
place shop: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input a_amt: money PLN
input t_amt: money PLN
input o_amt: money PLN
input o_day: date
input a_day: date
input t_day: date
def arrive[m in events, p in parties]: num at m.day
  rule base = (if p == ania then 1 else 0)
  rule t beats base = (if p == tomek then 1 else 0) when m in tomeks

move a1: transfers
  on a_day
  leg cash from world to konto amount a_amt
move t1: tomeks
  on t_day
  leg cash from world to konto amount t_amt
move out: transfers
  on o_day
  when bal(konto) > 0 PLN
  reads konto
  leg cash from konto to shop amount o_amt

ask q: bal(konto, 2026-03-01), bal(konto, 2026-03-01) of ania, bal(konto, 2026-03-01) of tomek

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  persons + [ania] lives 1980-01-01..
  persons + [tomek] lives 1981-01-01..
  opening[konto] = 0 PLN at 2026-01-01 start
  a_amt = 100.00 PLN
  t_amt = 50.00 PLN
  o_amt = 30.00 PLN
  o_day = 2026-03-01
  a_day = 2026-02-01
  t_day = 2026-02-02

version stmt
  cite s
  governs 2026-03
  known 2026-03-02
  pad konto from world
  stated[konto] = 100.00 PLN after out
=== expect
q: (100.00 PLN, 50.00 PLN, 50.00 PLN)
...
